{# Skill pack: subdomain_enum #}
## Skill: Subdomain Enumeration
applies_when: Use when the engagement includes a parent domain and its subdomains.
target_under_test: {{ target }}
difficulty_level: {{ difficulty_level }}

signals:
  - wildcard DNS pointing every name at one address
  - certificate transparency entries that list additional names
probe_order:
  1. Passive sources first: subfinder, amass passive mode
  2. Resolve collected names and keep only names inside scope
  3. Confirm live HTTP services with httpx before any deeper probe
  4. Add virtual-host discovery only when the target has a dedicated web front end
validation_criteria:
  - the name resolves and is inside the declared domain scope
  - a live service answers on the resolved name, or the name is a dangling record
evidence_required:
  - the resolver answer, the source of the name, and the HTTP status when live
constraints:
  - never enumerate or probe a parent domain that is not in scope
  - stop subdomain brute force once rate limits are reached
